			"label": "Articles (any time, not in the sequence)"
		},
		{
			"id": "phase4",
			"type": "group",
			"x": -24,
			"y": 2384,
			"width": 508,
			"height": 232,
			"color": "6",
			"label": "Phase 4 · Production"
		},
		{
			"id": "phase3",
			"type": "group",
			"x": -24,
			"y": 2086,
			"width": 508,
			"height": 188,
			"color": "5",
			"label": "Phase 3 · Safety"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 1 · [[Mine the corpus with the SLM]]\nThe fine-tuned extractor (held-out word F1 0.785, same field search as DeepSeek: 38 / 66 / 80) over all 512k documents; import and embed the fields. ≈ $9–13, Vast top-up first.\n**Unblocks:** field search over the whole corpus for the final evaluation.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 74,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 268,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 5 · [[Detect out-of-scope questions]]\nSay \"not found\" instead of answering: a 4th verdict, \"no document answers\", in the agent's check.\n**Done when:** 50–100 off-topic questions built in rerunnable rounds; refusal rates measured.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1458,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 240
		},
		{
			"id": "t5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 3 · [[Evaluate the full pipeline with clarifying questions]]\nThe final evaluation: benchmark + Slack dev set end to end, with ambiguous and multi-turn questions and the simulated person; repeated runs.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 750,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 212,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "title",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# Roadmap\n⬇ in order. The SLM is trained and scored (22 Nov): it searches as well as DeepSeek's labels. Now: mine the corpus, then the final evaluation.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": -260,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 4 · [[Rewrite the query from the chat history]]\nOne standalone query from the conversation before the first search; ask_user replies become filters (source, channel, team).\n**Done when:** multi-turn questions score like single questions.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1120,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 268
		},
		{
			"id": "a1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "[[Article - strategy for messier documents]]\nImages, tables, fragmented Slack dialogs: descriptive only.",
			"x": 660,
			"y": 64,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 124
		},
		{
			"id": "a2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "[[Article - problems by metric and how to fix them]]\nSymptom in the metrics → cause → fix, from articles 003–007.",
			"x": 660,
			"y": 218,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 152
		},
		{
			"id": "a3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "[[Article - future map]]\nOpen and stopped routes from the research maps, grouped.",
			"x": 660,
			"y": 400,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 124
		},
		{
			"id": "t6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 7 · [[Add guardrails]]\nPrompt injection in documents, access rules, personal data in answers; a small red-team set.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 2110,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 140
		},
		{
			"id": "t7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 6 · [[Measure pipeline speed and cost]]\nWall time per stage per question; p50 / p95 latency; $ per 1,000 questions.\n**Unblocks:** the production choices (rerank depth, pre-search gate).",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1768,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 184
		},
		{
			"id": "t8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## 8 · [[Add observability and RAG quality tracking]]\nTraces per request, chat metrics (follow-ups, rephrasing, not-found rate), alerts.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 2408,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 184
		},
		{
			"id": "t9",
			"type": "text",
			"color": "3",
			"width": 460,
			"height": 268,
			"x": 0,
			"y": 412,
			"text": "## 2 · [[Prepare the evaluation for the final run]]\nJudge rule (lenient, strict or both), comparability with run 31, memory notes; then field-agent and field-agent-clarify end to end.\n**Done when:** both systems have judged benchmark runs."
		},
		{
			"id": "a4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "[[Private and personal data questions]]\nSalary, vacation, HR records: not in this dataset; how a real deployment refuses or routes them.",
			"x": 660,
			"y": 560,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 124
		}
	],
